l,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.16705155487623147,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.18643721806711144,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0509425528358692,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":67.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.28617334705200426,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.014341590612777053,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":76.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.00765,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.1,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":10.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Columbia Banking System, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Columbia Bank that provides banking, private banking, mortgage, and other financial services in the United States. The company offers deposit products, including business, non-interest-bearing checking, interest-bearing checking and savings, money market, insured cash sweep and other investment sweep solutions, and certificates of deposit. It also provides commercial lending products, such as commercial lines of credit and term loans, accounts receivable and inventory financing, international trade finance, commercial property loans, multifamily loans, equipment loans, commercial equipment leases, real estate construction loans, permanent financing, small business administration program financing, and capital markets services. In addition, the company offers wealth management, comprising financial planning, investment, trust, insurance, and private banking solutions, as well as treasury management, which includes digital and mobile banking solutions, ACH, wires, positive pay, remote deposit capture, integrated payments, integrated receivables, lockbox, cash vault, real-time payments, commercial card, foreign exchange, trade and supply chain finance, international banking related products, and merchant services. Further, it provides residential real estate loans and consumer loans. The company serves corporate, institutional, small business, and individual customers in the United States. Columbia Banking System, Inc. was founded in 1953 and is based in Tacoma, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Clinton E. Stein CPA | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $383K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $118K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Columbia Banking System, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $8.7B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +47% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $706M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (90% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.1},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","22 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"COLB's $1.2B Buyback Plan Highlights Strong Capital Returns After Q3","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027884/colb-s-1-2b-buyback-plan-highlights-strong-capital-returns-after-q3?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_finance_sector-3027884","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794414480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Price-Driven Insight from (COLB) for Rule-Based Strategy","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/Price-Driven_Insight_from_COLB_for_Rule-Based_Strategy_111026011801_1794334681.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794334681.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Does Balance Sheet Remix Change The Bull Case For Columbia Banking System Stock (COLB)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-colb/columbia-banking-system/news/does-balance-sheet-remix-change-the-bull-case-for-columbia-b","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794093729.071,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Columbia Banking System raises dividend by 2.7% to $0.38","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4672335-columbia-banking-system-raises-dividend-by-27-to-038","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794576291.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"Columbia Banking System Announces Increase to Common Share Dividend","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/colu